            <ArticleTitle>Dactylitis in a child with sickle cell trait.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>814-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dactylitis commonly occurs in patients with homozygous hemoglobin S disease (sickle cell anemia), sickle cell-hemoglobin C disease or sickle cell-beta-thalassemia. A case is reported of dactylitis associated with sickle cell trait, a very rare occurrence. It may be that in this patient the disorder was secondary to severe diarrhea and dehydration.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
